2. COMPILER INTEGRITY, ANTI-TAMPERING & REPRODUCTION RESTRICTIONS:
The Cluster compiler, toolchain, and architecture belong exclusively to
Mohammad Zaid (GitHub: zk-mohammad) and the official Cluster Organization
(https://github.com/cluster-lang). 

To protect compiler integrity, user security, and eliminate rogue compiler attacks:
- Duplication, modification, patching, decompilation, binary surgery, or reverse
  engineering of the compiler software and binary is STRICTLY PROHIBITED.
- Producing derivative compiler binaries, releasing unauthorized binary clones,
  launching unauthorized forks, or redistributing rogue compiler distributions
  is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN.
- Exactly ONE canonical binary distribution exists, officially published under
  https://github.com/cluster-lang and https://github.com/zk-mohammad.
- All duplicate copies, modified binaries, unauthorized forks, or third-party
  distributions are strictly INVALID and unauthorized.
- Internal compiler source code is temporarily private and will be released
  publicly in an upcoming official release. Only official binary releases are
  authorized for beta testing.

3. COMMERCIAL USE RESTRICTIONS:
Any use of the Software, its compiler binary, runtime components, standard library,
